cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use AccuratePredict TRACE, please cite it as below."
title: "AccuratePredict TRACE: an open sports prediction algorithm for timestamped, calibrated forecasts"
type: software
authors:
  - name: "AccuratePredict"
    website: "https://accuratepredict.com"
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-11-21"
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/accuratepredict/accuratepredict-trace-sports-prediction-algorithm"
url: "https://accuratepredict.com"
abstract: >-
  TRACE (Timestamped, Ratings, Adjusted, Calibrated, Evaluated) is the sports
  prediction framework used by AccuratePredict. This reference implementation
  provides a time-decayed Dixon-Coles goals model, a margin-aware Elo rating,
  market de-vigging and blending, Platt calibration, a hash-chained
  prediction log and proper-scoring-rule evaluation, in dependency-free Python.
keywords:
  - sports prediction
  - football prediction model
  - Dixon-Coles
  - Elo rating
  - probability calibration
  - Brier score
  - forecasting
references:
  - type: article
    authors: [{family-names: Dixon, given-names: Mark J.}, {family-names: Coles, given-names: Stuart G.}]
    title: "Modelling association football scores and inefficiencies in the football betting market"
    journal: "Journal of the Royal Statistical Society: Series C"
    volume: 46
    issue: 2
    year: 1997
  - type: article
    authors: [{family-names: Maher, given-names: M. J.}]
    title: "Modelling association football scores"
    journal: "Statistica Neerlandica"
    volume: 36
    issue: 3
    year: 1982
